# Ramin Torabi <16882282+RaminTorabi@users.noreply.github.com> (2026-07-04)
# Anthropic Claude apps (prebuilt-binary repackages), hard-masked: shipped in
# the overlay so they can be pinned/installed on purpose, but never pulled in
# by a default emerge. They are proprietary (LICENSE=Anthropic-Claude-Terms)
# and Anthropic's Linux desktop app is a BETA packaged for Debian/Ubuntu.
# Unmask in /etc/portage/package.unmask/rato-verlay (and ACCEPT_LICENSE the
# Anthropic-Claude-Terms) to opt in.
dev-util/claude-code-bin
dev-util/claude-desktop-bin

# Ramin Torabi <16882282+RaminTorabi@users.noreply.github.com> (2026-08-16)
# dev-util/kirocrew-bin is NOT hard-masked. It was introduced masked on
# 2026-08-16 pending verification and unmasked the same day after a full
# verify run on cirrus: upstream fetch + Manifest hash check, a complete
# `ebuild clean install` (only the documented benign $ORIGIN soname QA
# notice), all install artefacts present (launcher, XDG entry, icon,
# setuid chrome-sandbox), and ldd against the bundled Electron binary
# resolving every DT_NEEDED from the declared RDEPEND. It stays
# keyworded ~amd64 (accept via package.accept_keywords), so consumers do
# NOT need a package.unmask entry - same shape as the other prebuilt
# Kiro packages (dev-util/kiro-bin, dev-util/kiro-cli-bin).

